#. Tag: title
#: rawconverter.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Raw Image Converter"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With this Kipi-plugin you can import/convert your images stored in "
"<emphasis>RAW format</emphasis> to three formats (<guilabel>JPEG</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>TIFF</guilabel>, <guilabel>PPM</guilabel>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are ome considerations before your convert, and even before you shoot "
"in raw format. RAW image file formats keep the original information of the "
"exposure supposedly without loss (when compressed, they use reversible, "
"lossless compressions algorithms). Many photographers prefer to take their "
"picture in RAW mode because the camera's built-in conversion program is "
"often of lesser quality than what you can achieve with digital image "
"processing. The whitebalance of the digital camera is registered but not "
"applied to the image. Some CMOS CCD's create four types of color filter "
"data: RGBG, Red, Green, Blue and another Green mask for contrast "
"enhancement. The plugin can take this into account."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The conversion is actually based on Dave Coffin's command line tool "
"<command>dcraw</command> (Dave: <quote>Don't expect dcraw to produce the "
"same images as software provided by the camera vendor. Sometimes dcraw gives "
"better results!</quote>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: rawconverter.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "Single Conversion Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the RAW file to convert and open the plugin from the host "
"application. The <emphasis>Raw Image Converter</emphasis> window in single "
"mode will appear. Click on <guilabel>Preview</guilabel> to show the effect "
"of your settings taking shape."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you can adjust the available check and value boxes to optimize the "
"conversion process. The first checkbox indicates to use the camera settings "
"for white balance. The essential parameters like brightness, and red/blue "
"amplifier may be adjusted. If the result is not quite optimal, don't worry, "
"it is always possible to fine-tune the image later on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A <guilabel>Four color RGBG</guilabel> conversion can be selected to use "
"contrast information. (If your camera works in RGB mode, the RGBG setting "
"has no effect)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you're happy with the preview, choose one of three output formats to save "
"the conversion result. The file name will stay the same, only the extension "
"changes. <guilabel>JPEG</guilabel> uses the lossy algorithm and produces the "
"smallest output file size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The tagged image format (<guilabel>TIFF</guilabel>) preserves all "
"information of your image while using lossless LZW compression."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Portable PixMap format (<guilabel>PPM</guilabel>) produces the largest "
"output file and contains most data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you intend to work a lot on your images or if it is likely that you have "
"to reuse it later on, then don't use <guilabel>JPEG</guilabel> format "
"because it allows a limited number of operations before it deterioates "
"visibly. <guilabel>TIFF</guilabel> and <guilabel>PPM</guilabel> are better "
"suited to keep the original data."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose <guilabel>JPEG</guilabel> as the <guilabel>Save Format</"
"guilabel> then the meta-data included in RAW file will be included in the "
"<guilabel>JPEG</guilabel> files as Exif information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you have finished click the <guibutton>Process</guibutton> button to "
"start the conversion. If you want abort image conversion, press the "
"<guibutton>Abort</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: rawconverter.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "The RAW Converter Dialog in Single Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: rawconverter.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Batch Conversion Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The batch mode converter allows you to convert several images in one go. Use "
"this mode when you're are sure of the best settings, &eg; try it out in "
"single conversion mode first."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: rawconverter.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The available setting are mostly identical to the single mode dialog. Here "
"you have the additional option to overwrite existing files (which you might "
"have created in an earlier try). The preview option is not available here. A "
"progress bar indicates the conversion status."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: rawconverter.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Batch RAW Converter Dialog"
msgstr ""
